# ============================================================================
# [REV-167b — REGISTER ENTRY 45 (TIER-3 VARIANT SELECTION, SPEC OF RECORD:
# docs/features/The Pose Pipeline - Full Audit & Improvement.md §5 D-3 Shape 1)]
# The DIALOGUE lane's variant decision call: the member action has already been
# picked by the main conversational model (the action yaml); this lightweight
# call picks the exact move within that pool from the tag-carrying corpus.
# The corpus ships CANDIDATE-FLAGGED (user ruling R-A: Cline's 12.6 candidate
# tags + descriptions apply as shipped; the user's entry-45 pen refinement is
# pending -- text-only fix by design).
# Output contract consumed by OnVariantPick in SkyrimNet_AnimationsGS.psc:
# "CLIP: <exact move key>" (e.g. "CLIP: GS9"). A miss/timeout/invalid key
# degrades to the shipped dice draw (D-5, byte-for-byte).
# ============================================================================

[ system ]
    You pick the exact move for a pose that has already been chosen. The
    category is fixed; your only job is WHICH variant of it this moment means.
    Match the wording of the request and the scene against each move's
    description -- the words are the contract (a "twerk" request wants the
    move that says twerk; a shy moment wants the move that says shy).

    Answer with EXACTLY one line, no preamble:
    CLIP: <exact move key>
    The key is the GS-number at the start of the matching entry (e.g. GS9).
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    ## Who is posing
    {{ npcName }}

    ## The pose being struck
    {{ label }} (pool: {{ vibe }})

    ## The exact moves in this pool (the key first)
    {{ variants }}

    ## Recent events (what just happened around here)
    {{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}

    Which move is this moment asking for?
[ end user ]
